1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:07,900
The install videos end at one audit file, on one machine. This is the other half.

2
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:14,000
Connect a workspace and every governed call lands in one feed.

3
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:20,000
One row per call: the tool, what it's allowed to do, the risk, and why.

4
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:26,300
Identity and latency on every row — and for model calls, the tokens and the cost.

5
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:32,800
Approvals is where a step-up policy sends blocked actions. Nothing here has executed.

6
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:37,000
Right now, nothing waiting. 31 approved, 1 rejected.

7
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,800
Back to the feed. This is every agent in the workspace, not one terminal.

8
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:55,500
Runs is one row per execution. Sort by cost and the expensive ones surface.

9
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:04,400
Open the top run and the money view breaks it apart.

10
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:09,300
The orchestration loop is 96% of the bill. Every Edit, Bash and Read call: free.

11
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:15,600
Real workspace, real traffic. Connect one and it starts filling in.
